/// WorkoutTrainer rotation for Liftosaur: L1 -> U1 -> L2 -> U2 -> L3 -> U3 -> L1 ...
/// Rendered 2026-10-21 from templates/6-day-week.md, templates/rotation.json and
/// templates/progression-tracks.md. Revised 2026-10-21 against the official Liftoscript
/// doc (https://www.liftosaur.com/doc/liftoscript), the grammar file and the built-in
/// exercise list on GitHub (research/mobile-workout-trackers.md, addendum
/// "official-source verification").
///
/// Comment rules used here (from the doc and the grammar): "///" lines are hidden notes.
/// "//" lines are descriptions SHOWN to the lifter: above an exercise they describe the
/// exercise, above a "## Day" header they describe the day. Comments are whole lines only;
/// nothing may follow an exercise on its line.
///
/// Units: kg. Starting loads are the worked example in guide/03-flexible-scheduling.md,
/// section 6 (squat 120, bench 85, deadlift 150, press 55, row 70, pull-up +10).
/// Replace them with yours: templates/progression-tracks.md, section 2.
///
/// H exposure = 1 x 4 top set @ RPE 8, then back-offs at -7% (3 in a split session;
/// deadlift 2). V exposure = sets at 90% of the lift's current top-set load, no top set.
/// Accessories = double progression: fixed load, reps up to the top of the range at
/// RPE 9 or less, then +2.5 kg (or one dumbbell step) and back to the bottom.
///
/// Rep ranges: every double-progression line is written at the BOTTOM of its range with
/// the range in dp(step, min, max), as in the doc's examples ("3x8 / progress: dp(5lb, 8, 12)").
/// The app adds one rep to every set after each exposure where all prescribed reps are
/// completed, and at the top of the range adds the step and returns to the bottom. So
/// "3x8 ... dp(2.5kg, 8, 10)" is the template's 3 x 8-10. Do not write "3x8-10" with
/// dp(): in a local run of Liftosaur's own code the range collapsed (8-10 became 10-10).
///
/// Progressions: one rule per exercise for the whole program (the doc: different
/// progressions for the same exercise are an error), and a step applies to every day
/// the exercise appears. A repeated accessory carries its rule on its first appearance
/// only and moves together on all its days. V exposures use the label "v:" so they are
/// separate exercises: the H track's lp()/dp() never moves them, and finishing a V day
/// never moves the track. "progress: none" is not enough for that: in the same local
/// run, an lp() step on Day 1 still raised an unlabelled copy marked "progress: none".
/// The Day 5 calf raise uses the label "hirep:" because its range differs.
///
/// Warm-ups: "ramp" = bar x 10, 40% x 8, 60% x 5, 80% x 2; "feeder" = 1 x 3 at 65%
/// (templates/rotation.json). Liftosaur warm-up percentages are of the FIRST working
/// set's weight, which on an H line is the top set. Accessories keep the app's default
/// warm-ups. Rest timers are the per-exercise values in templates/rotation.json.
/// Supersets follow the superset groups in templates/rotation.json.

# Week 1

// **Squat heavy.** Top set 4 @ RPE 8, back-offs at -7%; stop the back-offs if a set hits RPE 9.
// Accessories: double progression at RPE 9 or less. The app adds a rep after each session in which you complete the prescribed reps; at the top of the range it adds the smallest load step and goes back to the bottom. Log the reps you actually did.
// Swaps: leg press -> Bulgarian split squat; cable crunch -> hanging leg raise.
## Day 1: L1 Lower A (squat heavy)
/// Track: squat. lp() advances on completed reps only, not on the logged RPE (README, known gaps).
Squat / 1x4 120kg @8+, 3x4 112.5kg @7+ / 180s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80% / progress: lp(2.5kg)
Romanian Deadlift, Barbell / 3x8 @8+ / 150s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 8, 10)
Leg Press / 3x10 @8+ / 120s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 12)
Seated Leg Curl / 3x10 @9+ / 75s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)
Standing Calf Raise, Leverage Machine / 4x8 @9+ / 75s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 8, 12)
Cable Crunch / 3x10 @9+ / 60s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)

// **Bench heavy, row heavy.** Bench: top set 4 @ RPE 8, back-offs at -7%. Row: 4 x 6-8 at RPE 8; add 2.5 kg when every set reaches 8.
// Superset the lateral raise with the triceps extension.
## Day 2: U1 Upper A (bench heavy, row heavy)
/// Track: bench. 1 kg steps need 0.5 kg plates. Without them use lp(2.5kg, 2) (2.5 kg after
/// every second success, progression-tracks.md section 9) instead of lp(1kg).
Bench Press / 1x4 85kg @8+, 3x4 79kg @7+ / 180s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80% / progress: lp(1kg)
/// Track: row (double progression, 6-8 reps).
Bent Over Row / 4x6 70kg @8+ / 150s / warmup: 1x3 65% / progress: dp(2.5kg, 6, 8)
/// 2 kg = one dumbbell step; adjust to your rack.
Incline Bench Press, Dumbbell / 3x8 @8+ / 120s / progress: dp(2kg, 8, 12)
Lateral Raise, Dumbbell / 4x12 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2kg, 12, 20)
Triceps Extension, Cable / 3x10 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)
Face Pull / 3x15 @9+ / 60s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 15, 20)

// **Deadlift heavy.** Top set 4 @ RPE 8, 2 back-offs at -7%, 3-5 min rest after the top set. Crisp reps; no grinding.
// Lunge reps are per leg. Swaps: front squat -> hack squat; lunge -> Bulgarian split squat; back extension -> Pallof press.
## Day 3: L2 Lower B (deadlift heavy)
/// Track: deadlift. Two back-offs in every week type.
Deadlift / 1x4 150kg @8+, 2x4 140kg @7+ / 240s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80% / progress: lp(2.5kg)
Front Squat / 3x6 @8+ / 150s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 6, 10)
/// templates/6-day-week.md names a walking lunge; templates/rotation.json lists a reverse lunge first.
Lunge, Dumbbell / 3x8 @8+ / 120s / progress: dp(2kg, 8, 12)
/// Same exercise and same rule as Day 1, so the progression is not repeated here.
Seated Leg Curl / 3x10 @9+ / 75s / superset: A
Standing Calf Raise, Leverage Machine / 4x8 @9+ / 75s / superset: A
/// 45-degree back extension; any added load is the number on the line.
Back Extension, Bodyweight / 3x10 @8+ / 60s / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)

// **Press heavy, pull-up heavy.** Press: top set 4 @ RPE 8, back-offs at -7%. Pull-up: 4 x 5-8 at RPE 8; add 2.5 kg when every set reaches 8.
// The pull-up weight is the ADDED load (turn on "Bodyweight for Bar" in Me -> Equipment). Under 5 clean reps: use the lat pulldown until a set at about bodyweight reaches 8.
// Swaps: dumbbell bench -> dips.
## Day 4: U2 Upper B (press heavy, pull-up heavy)
/// Track: press. Same 1 kg note as the bench (lp(2.5kg, 2) without 0.5 kg plates).
Overhead Press / 1x4 55kg @8+, 3x4 51kg @7+ / 180s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80% / progress: lp(1kg)
/// Track: pull-up (double progression, 5-8 reps, added load).
Pull Up / 4x5 10kg @8+ / 150s / warmup: 1x3 65% / progress: dp(2.5kg, 5, 8)
Bench Press, Dumbbell / 3x8 @8+ / 120s / progress: dp(2kg, 8, 12)
/// Reverse pec deck.
Reverse Fly, Leverage Machine / 3x15 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 15, 20)
Lateral Raise, Cable / 3x12 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 12, 20)
Incline Curl / 3x10 @9+ / 75s / progress: dp(2kg, 10, 12)

// **Squat and deadlift volume** at 90% of each track load. No top set; no set past RPE 9. Deadlift sets crisp and fast (RPE 6-7).
// Swaps: hanging leg raise -> cable crunch or Pallof press.
## Day 5: L3 Lower C (squat volume, deadlift volume)
/// V: 90% of the squat track (120 x 0.9 = 108 -> 107.5). The "v:" label keeps it off the
/// track. Edit it to 90% of the new track when the Day 1 top set moves (README).
v: Squat / 4x6 107.5kg @8+ / 150s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80%
/// V: 90% of the deadlift track (150 x 0.9).
v: Deadlift / 3x4 135kg @7+ / 150s / warmup: 1x3 65%
Seated Leg Curl / 3x10 @9+ / 75s / superset: A
Leg Extension / 3x12 @9+ / 75s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 12, 15)
/// Different range from Days 1 and 3, so a separate exercise via the label.
hirep: Standing Calf Raise, Leverage Machine / 4x10 @9+ / 60s / superset: B / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)
Hanging Leg Raise / 3x10 @9+ / 60s / superset: B / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)

// **All four upper lifts at volume**, 90% of each track load. Bench 4 x 6 (RPE 7-8), press 3 x 5 (RPE 6-7), row 3 x 8-10, pull-up 3 x 6-8 at RPE 7.
// Run the last three as a circuit. Swaps: pushdown -> skullcrusher; machine preacher curl -> EZ-bar curl.
## Day 6: U3 Upper C (all four upper main lifts at volume)
/// V: 90% of the bench track (85 x 0.9).
v: Bench Press / 4x6 76.5kg @8+ / 150s / warmup: 1x10 20kg, 1x8 40%, 1x5 60%, 1x2 80%
/// V: 90% of the press track (55 x 0.9).
v: Overhead Press / 3x5 49.5kg @7+ / 120s / warmup: 1x3 65%
/// V: 90% of the row track (70 x 0.9 = 63 -> 62.5).
v: Bent Over Row / 3x8-10 62.5kg @8+ / 120s
/// V: added load reduced so the sets land at RPE 7 (0kg = bodyweight).
v: Pull Up / 3x6-8 5kg @7+ / 120s
Lateral Raise, Dumbbell / 3x12 @9+ / 60s / superset: A
Triceps Pushdown / 3x10 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 15)
Preacher Curl, Leverage Machine / 3x10 @9+ / 60s / superset: A / progress: dp(2.5kg, 10, 12)

/// End of the pass. Finishing a workout runs the progressions and advances to the next
/// program day whatever the calendar says (REST API doc: workout/finish "advance the day"),
/// so after Day 6 the program returns to Day 1. That is the rotation pointer.
